    "## Project Goal:\n",
    "FSHD is a progressive muscular disease that can cause muscle weakness and degeneration over time. However, because disease progression varies between individuals and can occur gradually, measuring these changes accurately is challenging in clinical trials.\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal of this project is to analyze FSHD patient data to compare MRI-derived muscle fat fraction and muscle strength measurements to find out which is more sensitive to disease progression. By examining how these measurements change over time, we want to identify which gives us a more consistent and reliable indication of muscle degeneration. Our findings will help us recommend which measurement may be more useful when evaluating new FSHD treatments in clinical trials.\n",
    "\n",
    "Research Question: Which is more sensitive to FSHD disease progression, MRI fat fraction or muscle strength?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "91408b75-185a-4d66-9ce7-7c7aabbde5e1",
